        "original_id": "14376477-79e4-5086-9e28-28fa772fb8e4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Andrew Fastow, Lea Fastow, Jeffrey Fastow, Matthew Fastow\n- Companies: Enron, LJM\n- Roles: Chief financial officer\n- Places: Houston, Texas\n- Concepts: Bankruptcy, fraud, ghost entities, financial statements\n\nFacts:\n- Andrew Stuart Fastow was born on December 22, 1961.\n- Andrew Fastow was the chief financial officer of Enron Corporation, an energy trading company based in Houston, Texas, until Enron fired him shortly before the company declared bankruptcy.\n- In 1999, Andrew Fastow created LJM, a company named for his wife Lea and his children Jeffrey and Matthew.\n- Andrew Fastow created LJM to buy Enron's poorly performing stocks and stakes and to bolster Enron's financial statements.\n- Andrew Fastow unlawfully maintained personal stakes in ostensibly independent ghost entities and thereby defrauded Enron out of tens of millions of dollars.",
